+## AGC 26.2 alpha12 - Thousand-player survival scale remodel
+
+Alpha12 shifts the performance target from mini-game-only density to ordinary survival density: thousands of players while preserving vanilla/Paper-visible semantics. The new rule is still no packet drops, no chunk FIFO head skipping, no entity tick skipping, no off-thread Bukkit mutation, and no plugin event reordering.
+
+New runtime layers:
+
+- `AGCSurvivalScaleCoordinator` - central mode planner for normal survival, dense survival, thousand-player survival, and hotspot control. It coordinates only invisible work: shared fanout preparation, read-only caches, global fairness and resource budgets.
+- `AGCResourceEfficiencyEngine` - CPU/memory-aware budget engine. It reserves CPU headroom for ordered commits, plugins, Netty, GC and the OS, then spends remaining budget on safe read-only/batch lanes.
+- `AGCInterestGraph` - tick-local player interest graph for dense hotspots. It deduplicates read-only packet/entity/chunk fanout preparation without hiding players, reducing view distance, or changing tracker semantics.
+- `AGCGlobalFairnessMatrix` - global deficit fairness across players, worlds, arenas and regions so a single hotspot cannot monopolize invisible work.
+- `AGCSharedReadOnlyCache` - tick-local cache for immutable derived computations. Entries clear every tick and never own live world state.
+
+New commands:
+
+- `/agc survival-scale` - shows survival mode, target players/TPS, interest graph, fairness and resource state.
+- `/agc resources` - shows CPU/memory-aware invisible work budget state.
+
+Plugin API additions:
+
+- `AGC.performance().resourceProfile(expectedPlayers, targetTps)`
+- `AGC.performance().survivalScalePlan(expectedPlayers, activeWorlds, estimatedLoadedChunks, estimatedEntities)`
+- `AGCResourceProfile`
+- `AGCSurvivalScalePlan`
+
+Important: alpha12 does not claim a synthetic benchmark number as guaranteed. It makes the algorithms stricter for the stated goal: use compute resources more efficiently while keeping gameplay and plugin compatibility semantics intact.
